# === ai-readiness-kg ===

# ── Secrets / environments ────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.venv
env/
venv/
ENV/

# ── Seldon / Claude Code working directories ──────────────────────────────
.claude/
.seldon/
handoffs/
.worktrees/
tmp/
# cc_tasks/ is intentionally TRACKED: task files are the work spec and travel
# with the repo (see icsp_notebook lineage).

# ── Corpus staging (harvester finds, pre-manifest; DD-003) ────────────────
# Documents are inert until an explicit manifest_add event. Staging never ships —
# except the committed run logs, which are provenance records, not staged content.
# (Ignore staging *contents*, not the dir node, so a specific file can be re-included.)
corpus/staging/*
!corpus/staging/pilot_adds_run_log.md
# candidate_register.jsonl is the COMMITTED corpus screening log (PRISMA-style in/out
# decisions; metadata only, no document content) — task bulk_acquisition_v2, Part 0.
!corpus/staging/candidate_register.jsonl

# ── Acquired corpus binaries (primary-source PDFs) ─────────────────────────
# Kept local, NOT committed to this public repo: some are third-party (arXiv author
# copyright). The provenance chain survives via each manifest entry's primary_url +
# content_hash + local_path (re-fetch + re-hash reproduces the file). Mirrors the
# icsp_notebook pattern for large/external source files.
corpus/pilot/
# Non-pilot acquired captures (Cisco methodology/instrument web printouts + merge
# components). Same rationale: third-party captures kept local; provenance in manifest.
corpus/cisco/
# Bulk-acquired corpus PDFs (candidate register). Same rationale: kept local, provenance
# (primary_url + content_hash) travels in the manifest.
corpus/bulk/
# Machine-visibility kernel captures (task 2026-08-21_v03_visibility_kernel). Same
# rationale: third-party pages/specs kept local; provenance (primary_url + sha256) in events.
corpus/kernel/
# 2026-08-24 source-triage captures (task 2026-08-24_source_triage). Same rationale.
corpus/triage/

# Corpus binaries for task 2026-08-29_crosswalk_operationalization §0. Same rule as every
# other corpus dir: the bytes stay local, provenance survives in events/batch-017.jsonl via
# primary_url + content_hash (CLAUDE.md, invariant 2).
corpus/crosswalk/

# Round-2 acquisition captures (task 2026-08-30_acquisition_round2 §3). Same rule as every
# other corpus dir: the bytes stay local, provenance survives in events/batch-020.jsonl via
# primary_url + content_hash (CLAUDE.md, invariant 2).
corpus/round2/

# G1 EVAL prior-art acquisitions (task 2026-09-02_g1_eval_prior_art §3). Same rule: bytes
# local, provenance (primary_url + content_hash) in events/batch-025.jsonl.
corpus/g1eval/

